<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/7th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Arab–Byzantine wars</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">629–1050s</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Arab–Byzantine wars were fought between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a> and the Arab <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliphates</a> and their successor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">emirates</a> from 629 into the 11th century. In the first decades the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabs">Arabs</a> took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-africa">North Africa</a> and besieged <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a>, most seriously in 717–718. The frontier then settled along the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taurus-mountains">Taurus Mountains</a>, where raiding continued until the Byzantines recovered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crete">Crete</a> (961), <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cilicia">Cilicia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antioch">Antioch</a> (969) in the 10th century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/arab-byzantine-wars.jpg" alt="Arab–Byzantine wars" width="320" height="164" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Greekfire-madridskylitzes1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
